{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":9,"prev":"491316b3fe5ffd5f01cd0e706cf16bb137b18c4bd7b3618333efffa0d1bdf650","at":"2026-10-01T07:07:52.944049Z","type":"llm_call","state":"adjudicate","iter":0,"node":"adjudicate","data":{"kind":"adjudicate","model":"codex/gpt-5.6-sol","effort":"medium","index":0,"input_hash":"f57868f40c802189bb15908c8e79ade0fa7096590437d5a4f69f4c15fb600493","verdict":{"reasoning":"The finding is valid. `stop_guard_writable` verifies ownership and permissions only on the leaf `stop-gate` directory, then `stop_guard_file` returns a pathname that is written later. If an attacker owns or can write `/tmp/metareview`, they can rename or replace the validated leaf after the check and redirect the subsequent state-file access, potentially planting counters that cause an early stand-down. The sticky bit on `/tmp` does not protect entries inside an attacker-owned `/tmp/metareview`. This contradicts the code's stated protection against counter planting in the temp fallback.","is_real":true,"confidence":0.98},"confidence":0.98,"tokens":{"input":21480,"cache_read":0,"cache_create":0,"output":140,"reasoning":476},"duration_ms":19145}}
{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":10,"prev":"296e9d4324bb66a67cf090e3015f2642b32606fdd17fad816425a9812e3b2fc6","at":"2026-10-01T07:08:05.744151Z","type":"llm_call","state":"adjudicate","iter":0,"node":"adjudicate","data":{"kind":"adjudicate","model":"codex/gpt-5.6-sol","effort":"medium","index":1,"input_hash":"f83807f3dfbbe48979834847943c4aa5d8c29fa1b4a2e6e4d89dda849c2de347","verdict":{"reasoning":"The path is concrete: stop_guard_file returns 1 if all three candidate directories fail creation or stop_guard_writable, and block_is_repeat immediately returns 1 without persisting a count. Every subsequent refusal therefore blocks again indefinitely. This contradicts the change’s core claim that the host-independent guard bounds persistent loops, even though other comments acknowledge the fail-closed behavior. A read-only private cache plus an insecure shared Git directory and pre-planted temp directory is sufficient to trigger it.","is_real":true,"confidence":0.97},"confidence":0.97,"tokens":{"input":21482,"cache_read":0,"cache_create":0,"output":118,"reasoning":381},"duration_ms":12785}}
{"schemaVersion":1,"seq":11,"prev":"b10163cf13d6650929f5712cffab389c436b1e35ac24475299c8cf4d012e2a48","at":"2026-10-01T07:08:05.749186Z","type":"node_output","state":"adjudicate","iter":0,"node":"adjudicate","data":{"output":{"confirmed":[{"id":"847da5b25de4","desc":"[ADVISORY] stop_guard_file validates only the leaf stop-gate dir, not its parent, so an attacker controlling a world-writable parent could replace the leaf between check and write (TOCTOU). Narrow fail-open only where the fallback is /tmp/metareview.","file":"hooks/pre-finish.sh","line":148,"verdict":"real_but_ungold","confidence":0.98},{"id":"d17a28b111b8","desc":"[ADVISORY] When no state directory qualifies (rejected private cache, group-writable git dir, hostile temp dir), block_is_repeat returns 1 and that refusal path is unbounded. On a no-session host in a group-shared repo with no writable private state dir, the Stop hook could refuse forever; documented as failing toward blocking.","file":"hooks/pre-finish.sh","line":169,"verdict":"real_but_ungold","confidence":0.97}],"rejected":[]}}}
